A facet response for the regions facet: one region, West Virginia.

ASSEMBLED to the documented facet shape; see facet-authorities.source for the structure, the vendor
citations, and what each count level means. The region reuses the one embedded in
standard-full-fields.json so a test can prove the facet detail and the embedded copy agree.

What this fixture is for specifically:
  - ABFacetNames.Regions is "document.publication.regions", and GetRegionFacetAsync projects each
    detail into Region.
  - Region.Type is "state" here. It is an open string, not an enum: section 7.3 lists Region.Type
    alongside Standard.Status and ABEvent.ChangeType as a value whose complete set AB Connect has never
    published. A test should treat "state" as one observed value, not as the value set.
  - Region.Description is mapped from "descr". Region is the type where this mattered most: before
    version 3 it alone exposed the raw property name Descr while Authority, Publication, Document,
    StandardSection, and StandardStatement all mapped it to Description
    (01-sdk-v3.md section 7.4). A test that reads Description off this fixture pins that repair.
  - GetRegionFacetAsync has no CLI caller today. It is retained because it is one of the documented
    facets and costs one method, so this fixture is the only coverage it will get.
